# No Em Dashes in Responses

Never use em dashes (—) in any agent response, explanation, commit message, PR description, or other written output to the user.

## Prefer instead

- Commas
- Periods / separate sentences
- Colons
- Parentheses
- Hyphens (-) only when grammatically appropriate for compounds

## Examples

Bad: The API failed — check the logs.
Good: The API failed. Check the logs.
Good: The API failed: check the logs.
Good: The API failed (check the logs).

Do not replace an em dash with a double hyphen (--) as a workaround. Rewrite the sentence so no dash is needed.
